{
	"addonId": "newsHub",
	"displayName": "NewsHub for NVDA",
	"URL": "https://github.com/aris9952/newsHub/releases/download/v1.3.0/newsHub-1.3.0.nvda-addon",
	"description": "Reading news from various national and international news portals such as kompas.com, detik.com, and others is truly enjoyable. Aside from providing reliable information, it also broadens our knowledge as readers.\nHowever, as we know, the web pages of these news portals are not friendly to screen readers.\nThere are many advertisements and complex navigation elements that make reading difficult.\nThat is why \"NewsHub For NVDA\" is here!\n\nWith this add-on, you can read news from trusted news portals easily and comfortably. In this version, the add-on supports Kompas.com (23 rubrics), Detik.com (27 rubrics), CNN Indonesia (8 rubrics), CNBC Indonesia (7 rubrics), and Tempo.co (11 rubrics), complete with cross-portal keyword search, an accessible HTML reading view with NVDA Browse Mode navigation, and inline HTML5 photo and video playback (<video> and <img>) directly inside the article view.\nHappy reading!\n\nKeyboard Shortcuts:\n- NVDA+Shift+K: Open the NewsHub for NVDA dashboard from anywhere.\n- Ctrl+F: Jump to the cross-portal keyword search box.\n- Tab / Shift+Tab: Navigate between controls in the dashboard.\n- Up / Down Arrow: Select a news site, rubric, or article title, or read article content in the HTML viewer.\n- H / K / T / G / L: Navigate headings, links, tables, graphics, and lists in the HTML article reading area (NVDA Browse Mode).\n- Alt+[: Navigate to the previous article in the active list.\n- Alt+]: Navigate to the next article in the active list.\n- F5: Refresh the article list for the active rubric or search.\n- Ctrl+R: Reload the full content of the currently selected article.\n- Alt+R: Return focus to the rubric selection control.\n- Alt+S: Return focus to the news site selection control.\n- Escape: Clear active search results and restore the default view, or contextually return to the previous stage / close the dashboard.",
	"sha256": "83c7bb3459c48db300ad412c22386a5721cc62ad5b3d351b9a48b36fca1ab188",
